  "title": "Establish progressive usage calibration and autonomy policy",
  "state": "build",
  "owner_position": "developer",
  "assigned_agent_id": "agent-rikku",
  "created_at": "2026-08-31T13:20:59.516Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-31T13:25:06.459Z",
  "scope": [
    "Implement the data-driven Usage Protocol v2 foundation: project-local learning, a cold-start seed policy, progressive calibration states, evidence-gated routing modes, versioned cost provenance, and an exception-only autonomy envelope. No live model generation or external write is authorized."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Newly initialized and upgraded projects receive a project-owned usage policy with explicit seed, calibration, privacy, budget, and autonomy boundaries.",
    "Usage reporting reads the project policy, exposes calibration status, and keeps model recommendations in shadow or advisory mode until project evidence satisfies configured criteria.",
    "Routine in-envelope decisions do not require per-task approval; only enumerated risk, authority, privacy, cost, and confidence exceptions require human approval.",
    "Token ceilings are documented as runtime safety guards rather than monetary limits, and Credits or cost remain unknown without a configured versioned source.",
    "Focused tests, schema validation, Doctor, and the repository verification suite pass without a live model call."
  ],
